==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 4~16 seconds<sup>120f~480f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 10.67 seconds<sup>320f</sup>, delay 13.33~40 seconds<sup>400f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 0.07~16 seconds<sup>2f~480f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Emperor Santa]] spawns as the boss.
**50 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
**6 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.
**2 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Dark Emperor Santa has half the health of [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], but it will almost certainly perma-freeze your cats. [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] and [[Maiden Cat (Rare Cat)|Wrestling Cat]] will both be helpful as they are [[Immune to Freeze|immune to freeze]].

For the strategy, stall until you have a full wallet. When you finally hit the base, kill the Kang Roos and Doge Darks as soon as possible. When they're dead, you can time your speedy units (such as [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]] and [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow Cat]]) to whittle Dark Emperor Santa's health down.

Note that [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] will OHKO the Nyandam, so time him well.

